A||||6||Swany||running power wire to interior for an amp||||1||
Z||000000||Swany||07-07-2001||12:16 AM||||Hey guys,.. <P>Well, the project tonight is to run the power lead ,for my bass tube amp, (thanks again FieroGTguy) from the battery(in the back) to the interior. <P>I did a search and found a topic on this,... RogerGarrison posted ,to run the power wire along the top of the fire wall and try to fit the wire though an existing hole that a wiring harness is already passing though. <P>Well, I checked it out, and think this will be my best shot to do it with out drilling. Question is, where does it come out on the other side? as in, how much of the back of the interior do I have to take apart? I have the hayes manual, and I'm sure you guys know, its a real piece of crap. <P>Or.. if there is a better way? I'm open to suggestions.. <P>Thanks guys.. <P>On another note,probally not the best place for this but figured while I was posting.. <P>I've had my car for about a month now, and love it.. hope to have some pics up soon.. and I love the forum,.. I read it everyday.. even though I haven't posted much.. best resource I've found for my car, period.. I am so glad that Eds guy didn't ruin it for all of us. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||sqoach||07-07-2001||12:27 AM||||I found it pretty easy to drill a hole. I drilled mine with a 1/4" bit right between the two main wiring harnesses. Just take out the middle console. My amp kit came with a plastic grommet that fits in the hole so the wire doesn't get cut or ground out. I can get a pic if you'd like. Was pretty easy to do.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumsig.JPG">      <BR>84 SE (FOR SALE)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)(take it off my hands for $50)<BR>86 SC (FOR SALE sometime in this summer)<BR>86 SE V6 (new project)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Swany||07-07-2001||12:38 AM||||probably will have to drill,.. my biggest wonder was what I had to take out of the interior to get to the other side.. the center console, or more.. thanks for the help.. :-)||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierofreek2001||07-07-2001||12:40 AM||||Swany,  i ran my power lead from my battery to my amp by running it through one of the 3 holes that is directly under the ECM computer ( they are for the shift cables) behind the center console...  it worked perfectly..i didnt have to drill or anything... now the prob is that i believe it does make a buzzing noise, but a sound filter from radio shack will take care of that for sure... worked perfect for me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  check into it, i think u will be pleased that u dont have to drill anything<BR>steve<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennockssig.jpg"> <BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI> "Unofficial Pace Car"<BR><LI> 86 Fiero GT<BR></UL>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Swany||07-07-2001||01:07 AM||||that sounds interesting too.. guess the first step will be to remove the center console and have a look.. then, pick a hole to try, or drill.. <P>thanks again for the help.. will let ya know how it turns out..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Swany (edited 07-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tom88gt||07-07-2001||12:44 PM||||I drilled a hole right behine the battery.  It comes out near the top of the rear fire wall behind the carpeted pad/cover and runs down and along the lower door trim.||||reg||3
Z||000006||grinthock||07-07-2001||12:46 PM||||God why do it the hard way!  Both my Fiero's I have just pushed it through the shifter cable hole.. it's NICE a big has a NICE big grommet that stays nicely sealed... It works perfect.....<P>||||reg||1
